          "text": "YEN Ch'ang-ming 嚴長明 (T. 冬友, 東有, H. 道甫), 1731–1787, man of letters, was a native of Nanking, Kiangsu. As a boy, through the recommendation of Li Fu [q. v.], he studied under Fang Pao [q. v.] and Yang Shêng-wu 楊繩武 (T. 文叔, chin-shih of 1713).",
